Structure","description":"code-structure","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"c88f8f2d-adc5-4b22-adf0-baa1572b57ea","reference_count":0,"id":"7b2e9f38-2da3-4a87-8ccd-20cfbf5ba743","gmt_create":"2026-10-27T15:56:52.333515383+05:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-27T15:56:52.336161046+05:00"},{"catalog_id":"5a5674ea-0760-4e5e-9440-aef23c4e459e","title":"Project Overview","description":"project-overview","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"c88f8f2d-adc5-4b22-adf0-baa1572b57ea","reference_count":0,"id":"a11fa980-3469-4c2e-9ec0-48a23da8ba64","gmt_create":"2026-10-27T15:56:54.251482014+05:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-27T15:56:54.254369776+05:00"},{"catalog_id":"1e4c57bf-e141-4e07-b5bb-ff75c314ffd9","title":"Technical Implementation","description":"technical-implementation","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"c88f8f2d-adc5-4b22-adf0-baa1572b57ea","reference_count":0,"id":"a7d7a5e8-e994-41ff-a244-bc2c63da7029","gmt_create":"2026-10-27T15:57:06.252110733+05:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-27T15:57:06.260257316+05:00"},{"catalog_id":"4e348ab9-1fbf-458c-80ed-ff62e048bb7e","title":"Customization Guide","description":"customization-guide","extend":"{}","progress_status":"completed","repo_id":"c88f8f2d-adc5-4b22-adf0-baa1572b57ea","reference_count":0,"id":"5e0bb865-f5d6-44c9-aca0-0a163446f0bb","gmt_create":"2026-10-27T15:57:18.253112541+05:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-27T15:57:18.258508921+05:00"}],"wiki_overview":{"content":"\u003cblog\u003e\n# Project Analysis: umidjon_nuraliyev\n\n## 1. Project Introduction\n\n### Purpose Statement\nThis is a simple static HTML project that serves as a basic web page with Uzbek language support. The project appears to be a personal or portfolio-style website, featuring a greeting message in Uzbek (\"Assalomu alykum\" - meaning \"Hello\" in Uzbek).\n\n### Core Goals and Objectives\n- Provide a clean, minimal web presence\n- Support Uzbek language content\n- Demonstrate responsive web design principles\n- Serve as a foundation for potential expansion\n\n### Target Audience\n- Personal visitors or clients\n- Portfolio viewers\n- Users accessing the site from various devices\n\n## 2. Technical Architecture\n\n### Component Breakdown\nThe project follows a minimalist architecture with a single-page structure:\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    A[index.html] --\u003e B[HTML Structure]\n    A --\u003e C[Inline CSS Styles]\n    B --\u003e D[Main Content Area]\n    C --\u003e E[Responsive Design]\n    D --\u003e F[Uzbek Greeting Message]\n```\n\n### Design Patterns\n- **Single Page Application (SPA) Pattern**: Simple one-page layout\n- **Mobile-First Responsive Design**: Uses viewport meta tag and flexible typography\n- **CSS Grid Layout**: Modern grid-based centering approach\n- **Semantic HTML5**: Proper use of semantic elements like `\u003cmain\u003e`\n\n### System Relationships\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Client[Browser] --\u003e HTML[HTML Document]\n    HTML --\u003e CSS[Inline Styles]\n    HTML --\u003e Content[Content Layer]\n    Content --\u003e Text[Uzbek Text]\n```\n\n## 3. Key Implementation\n\n### Main Entry Points\n- **index.html**: Single entry point containing all HTML structure, styling, and content\n\n### Core Modules\n- **HTML Structure**: Semantic markup with proper document hierarchy\n- **CSS Styling**: Inline styles with modern CSS features including:\n  - CSS Grid for layout\n  - `clamp()` function for responsive typography\n  - Custom properties and modern selectors\n\n### Configuration Approach\n- **Meta Configuration**: \n  - UTF-8 character encoding for Uzbek text support\n  - Viewport configuration for mobile responsiveness\n  - Language attribute set to Uzbek (`lang=\"uz\"`)\n\n### External Dependencies\n- **No external dependencies**: Pure HTML/CSS implementation\n- **System fonts**: Uses Georgia and Times New Roman as fallback fonts\n\n### Integration Points\n- **Unicode Support**: Full Unicode support for Uzbek characters\n- **Cross-browser Compatibility**: Standard HTML5 and CSS3 features\n\n### Component Relationship Diagrams\n```mermaid\nclassDiagram\n    class HTMLDocument {\n        +DOCTYPE declaration\n        +html element\n        +head section\n        +body section\n    }\n    \n    class StyleSheet {\n        +body styles\n        +h1 styles\n        +responsive typography\n    }\n    \n    class ContentLayer {\n        +main element\n        +heading element\n        +Uzbek greeting\n    }\n    \n    HTMLDocument --\u003e StyleSheet\n    HTMLDocument --\u003e ContentLayer\n    ContentLayer --\u003e StyleSheet\n```\n\n## 4. Key Features\n\n### Functionality Overview\n- **Responsive Typography**: Dynamic font sizing using CSS `clamp()` function\n- **Centered Layout**: Perfect centering using CSS Grid\n- **Language Support**: Full Uzbek language support with proper encoding\n- **Mobile Optimization**: Viewport configuration for mobile devices\n\n### Implementation Highlights\n- **Modern CSS Features**: Utilizes contemporary CSS capabilities\n- **Accessibility**: Semantic HTML structure for better accessibility\n- **Performance**: Minimal overhead with no external resources\n\n### Feature Architecture Diagram\n```mermaid\nstateDiagram-v2\n    [*] --\u003e LoadPage\n    LoadPage --\u003e RenderStyles\n    RenderStyles --\u003e DisplayContent\n    DisplayContent --\u003e ResponsiveLayout\n    ResponsiveLayout --\u003e [*]\n    \n    state ResponsiveLayout {\n        [*] --\u003e MobileView\n        [*] --\u003e DesktopView\n        MobileView --\u003e DesktopView\n        DesktopView --\u003e MobileView\n    }\n```\n\n## 5. Conclusion and Recommendations\n\n### Project Architecture Summary\nThis is a minimalist, well-structured HTML project that demonstrates modern web development practices. The single-file architecture keeps the project simple while providing a solid foundation for expansion.\n\n### Key Characteristics\n- **Simplicity**: Clean, maintainable codebase\n- **Standards Compliance**: Follows HTML5 and CSS3 standards\n- **Accessibility**: Semantic markup and proper language attributes\n- **Performance**: No external dependencies for fast loading\n\n### Architectural Strengths\n- Minimal complexity reduces maintenance overhead\n- Responsive design ensures cross-device compatibility\n- Clean separation of concerns within single file\n- Proper internationalization support\n\n### Potential Improvement Areas\n- **Modularization**: Consider separating CSS into external stylesheet\n- **JavaScript Enhancement**: Add interactivity if needed\n- **SEO Optimization**: Add meta tags for search engine optimization\n- **Asset Management**: Organize images and other resources\n\n### Actionable Recommendations\n1. **Expand Content**: Add more sections beyond the greeting\n2. **Add Navigation**: Implement navigation structure for multi-page content\n3. **Enhance Styling**: Move CSS to external file for better organization\n4. **Add Interactivity**: Incorporate JavaScript for dynamic features\n5. **Optimize Performance**: Implement caching strategies and asset optimization\n\n### Next Steps for Project Evolution\n- **Content Development**: Build out additional pages and content\n- **Design System**: Establish consistent design patterns and components\n- **Testing Framework**: Add testing for cross-browser compatibility\n- **Deployment Strategy**: Set up hosting and deployment pipeline\n\nSources:\n- [index.html](index.html)\n\n\u003c/blog\u003e","gmt_create":"2026-10-27T15:55:52.827114904+05:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-27T15:55:52.827115047+05:00","id":"b78667a0-5281-490b-92dd-894223eadbf9","repo_id":"c88f8f2d-adc5-4b22-adf0-baa1572b57ea"},"wiki_readme":{"content":"No readme file","gmt_create":"2026-10-27T15:55:35.903818581+05:00","gmt_modified":"2026-10-27T15:55:35.903818684+05:00","id":"4bb37c49-e8ac-4e18-bde8-885f8f438938","repo_id":"c88f8f2d-adc5-4b22-adf0-baa1572b57ea"},"wiki_repo":{"id":"c88f8f2d-adc5-4b22-adf0-baa1572b57ea","name":"nuraliyev_umidjon","progre